# Reviewed benign-divergence allowlist for the recorded-target equivalence gate
# (ADR-001, slice 08). Each entry tolerates ONE specific benign divergence
# between the wezterm-term oracle (bare) and gutter's vt100 (wrapped) on the
# settled frame of tests/fixtures/claude-code-flow.cast at width 80.
#
# wezterm is a divergence CLASSIFIER, not pass/fail ground truth: a benign
# divergence is one where BOTH emulators rendered the same CHARACTER and only an
# SGR convention differs. Such a cell is tolerated ONLY if it appears here, with
# a human sign-off (this file is a reviewed, version-controlled diff).
#
# Format (whitespace-separated, one per line):
#   <row> <col> <bare_contents> <wrapped_contents>
# where `~` stands for an empty (blank) cell. Lines starting with `#` and blank
# lines are ignored.
#
# As of the slice-08 review the two emulators agree on EVERY cell of the
# fixture's settled frame — zero corrupting AND zero benign divergences — so no
# entry is required. The file exists, is consulted by the gate, and is the seam
# a reviewer adds to when a future fixture refresh surfaces a benign convention
# difference. The allowlist_load_bearing test proves an entry is honoured.
